# Line endings are decided by the repository, not by each machine.
#
# core.autocrlf is a per-machine setting and defaults to true in Git for
# Windows, which makes a checkout on a windows working copy CRLF while the same
# repository edited from WSL writes LF. The consequence is not cosmetic: a local
# `gofmt -l` then reports almost every file as unformatted, which hides the
# files that genuinely are.
#
# eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf for this repository, for everyone who clones it.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
